  "text_md": "Table II:\n\n<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th> </th>\n    <th>sandwich</th>\n    <th>brickwork</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>excitation energy</td>\n    <td>E a 2 . 522 ± 0 . 014 eV</td>\n    <td>2 . 565 ± 0 . 010 eV</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>excitation energy</td>\n    <td>E b 2 . 523 ± 0 . 014 eV</td>\n    <td>2 . 561 ± 0 . 010 eV</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>excitonic coupling V</td>\n    <td>exc 0 . 25 ± 0 . 017 eV</td>\n    <td> </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>center-center distance</td>\n    <td> </td>\n    <td>8.33 +</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>angle between long</td>\n    <td>6.0 + 1.70</td>\n    <td>34 . 0 ± 4 . 0 o</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>angle between short</td>\n    <td> </td>\n    <td>o 122 . 0 ± 3 . 9 o</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>distance of charge centers</td>\n    <td> </td>\n    <td>7 . 57 Å</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n\n# V. FIGURE CAPTIONS:\n\n# Figure 1:\n\nThe atom numbering for PIC is shown as it is used to tabulate the parameters\n\n# Figure 2:\n\nThe experimental absorption spectrum 4 of monomeric PIC (dots) is compared with a calculated spectrum (full line) from the displaced oscillator model. The calculated spectrum was shifted to reproduce the absorption maximum at 19100 cm − 1\n\n# Figure 3:\n\nStarting from a sandwich (a) or brickwork (b) structure relative stable dimer conﬁgurations evolved. The ﬁgure shows representative snapshots.\n\n",
